{"id":2234,"date":"2021-03-02T14:50:41","date_gmt":"2021-03-02T14:50:41","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=person&#038;p=2234"},"modified":"2025-11-01T14:39:36","modified_gmt":"2025-11-01T14:39:36","slug":"charlene-asiedu","status":"publish","type":"person","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/person\/charlene-asiedu\/","title":{"rendered":"Charlene Asiedu"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover profile-banner bg-alt\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim-100 has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:none\"><\/span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n\n\n<a href=\"javascript:history.back()\"> <div class=\"profiles-btn\"> \n\n<div class=\"btn-left-sq bg-primary\"> <i class=\"fa fa-caret-left white-text\"> <\/i> <\/div>\n<div class=\"btn-text title-bold white-text\">Back to Profiles<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/a>\n\n<h2 class=\"profile-name\">Charlene Asiedu<\/h2>\n\n<ul class=\"profile-list prof-pos\" style=\"list-style:none;\"><li class=\"profile-position\">Communications Officer<\/li><\/ul>\n\n<p class=\"profile-info profile-tagline primary-bold prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5 profile-body\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-11-01-at-14.38.02_52e62cf0.jpg\"\/>\n\n\n<p>Charlene Asiedu holds a Master&#8217;s Degree in International Affairs (Relations) from the Legon Centre for International Affairs and Diplomacy &#8211; LECIAD, University of Ghana (UG). Her undergraduate background is in liberal arts; including communications in language studies where she was awarded a year-abroad scholarship by UG, to increase Arabic language proficiency at Ain Shams University \u2013 Egypt.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Prior to joining AIMS, Charlene worked as a Teaching Assistant at UG and interned briefly with several institutions including the African Regent Hotel, Ghana Oil Company- GOIL and Ghana\u2019s Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Regional Integration (MFARI) building her capacity in communication skills. Charlene is a member of the communications committee of the Global Shapers Community (Accra Hub) which is a youth wing of the World Economic Forum (WEF).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Building knowledge in science communication, she handles content creation surrounding activities at the AIMS Ghana Centre, website and social media management, graphic and event venue design coordination, report writing as well as press engagement with mainstream media.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Charlene Asiedu holds a Master&#8217;s Degree in International Affairs (Relations) from the Legon Centre for International Affairs and Diplomacy &#8211; LECIAD, University of Ghana (UG). Her undergraduate background is in liberal arts; including communications in language studies where she was awarded a year-abroad scholarship by UG, to increase Arabic language proficiency at Ain Shams University<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":4,"featured_media":13152,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":"","profile-name":"Charlene Asiedu","profile-position":"Communications Officer","profile-tagline":""},"tags":[],"people_types":[12],"acf":[],"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-11-01-at-14.38.02_52e62cf0.jpg","coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/adel\/","display_name":"adel"},"relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 5 years ago","modified":"Updated 3 weeks ago"},"absolute_dates":{"created":"Posted on March 2, 2021","modified":"Updated on November 1, 2025"},"absolute_dates_time":{"created":"Posted on March 2, 2021 2:50 pm","modified":"Updated on November 1, 2025 2:39 pm"},"featured_img_caption":